  "description": "The SGM P-5W is a static LED wash with a rectangular housing about 0.50 m wide, 0.20 m deep and 0.19 m high, probably. A yoke bracket with side trunnions sits under a manual tilt hinge, clamped at the rear, and a manual pan hinge turns the whole unit on the base. Both hinges declare 360-degree travel but lack DMX control. The head has rear heatsink fins, a central tube with three round vent grilles, and cable glands and XLR connectors. The front is a recessed panel of 44 round LED lens domes in a 4-by-11 square grid, rows aligned, inside a narrow dark frame. The whole fixture is one intensity cell, with strobe and shutter acting fixture-wide.",
